 .gitignore                  |  8 ++++++++
 Gemfile                     |  5 +++++
 README.md                   | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++----
 _drafts/paper-template.html |  3 ++-
 4 files changed, 36 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 .gitignore
 create mode 100644 Gemfile

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8efd331
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# Files generated by the local preview (jekyll serve)
+_site/
+.jekyll-cache/
+.jekyll-metadata
+.sass-cache/
+vendor/
+Gemfile.lock
+.DS_Store
diff --git a/Gemfile b/Gemfile
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..511279d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Gemfile
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# Only used for previewing the site on your own computer.
+# GitHub Pages builds the live site by itself and ignores this file.
+source "https://rubygems.org"
+
+gem "jekyll", "~> 4.3"
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index a37da8e..0759379 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -13,8 +13,25 @@ GitHub Pages rebuilds the site within a minute or two. The homepage list (newest
 the post header and the contents sidebar are generated automatically, so `index.html`
 never needs editing.
 
-## Previewing locally
+## Previewing locally (no commit needed)
 
-The homepage is built by GitHub, so opening `index.html` directly shows template code
-instead of the list. To preview before pushing, install Jekyll and run
-`jekyll serve` in this folder, then open http://localhost:4000.
+One-time setup on macOS (needs [Homebrew](https://brew.sh)):
+
+```bash
+brew install ruby
+echo 'export PATH="$(brew --prefix)/opt/ruby/bin:$PATH"' >> ~/.zshrc
+source ~/.zshrc
+bundle install          # run inside this folder
+```
+
+Then, whenever you want to work on the site:
+
+```bash
+bundle exec jekyll serve --livereload
+```
+
+Open http://localhost:4000. Every time you save a file the site rebuilds and the
+browser refreshes. Stop the server with Ctrl+C.
+
+Don't use VS Code's Live Server for this site: it doesn't run Jekyll, so you'll see
+template code like `{% for post in site.posts %}` instead of the post list.
diff --git a/_drafts/paper-template.html b/_drafts/paper-template.html
index 91e5fe7..a5a274d 100644
--- a/_drafts/paper-template.html
+++ b/_drafts/paper-template.html
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 ---
 layout: post
-title: Paper Title
+title: "Paper Title"
 authors: Original Authors
 topic: Topic Tag
 paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/0000.00000
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/0000.00000
      e.g. _posts/2026-10-13-fitzpatrick-functions.html
      (the date in the file name is the date shown on the homepage)
   2. Fill in the lines between the --- marks above. "paper" is optional.
+     Keep the title in quotes: titles with a colon break without them.
   3. Write your notes below. The page header, contents sidebar and the
      homepage list are all generated for you.
 
